CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty struct has size >= 1: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [class]/4 + [expr.sizeof]/2: a complete object of class type has
NONZERO size; g++/clang give sizeof(empty) == 1.  CBMC lays empty
classes out with size 0.  MEASURED (round 118): adding the single
padding byte in typecheck_compound_type breaks 46 tests (empty
closures, decltype packs, EBO-adjacent shapes) -- the tool models
zero-sized empty classes self-consistently, so the fix needs a
coordinated layout change (padding byte + every consumer that assumes
empty classes are zero-sized), not a point patch.  Split from the
round-118 perfect-forward investigation, where sizeof(closure) >= 1
failed for an empty closure struct.
